    "explanation": "To both parties: this was a RYDE_POOL trip (TRP-00527). POL-RD-12 fixes the route-deviation baseline for a pooled trip at the platform's matched-itinerary optimal of 58.4 km recorded at match time (routing engine: pooled itinerary POOL-7731, 4 riders), not the 32.4 km solo figure, which the record carries only as solo_optimal_distance_km for reference. Measured on the governing trace figure of 60.91 km (EV-GPS-00527), the excess over that baseline is 2.51 km, or 4.30% of optimal. POL-RD-01 requires BOTH establishment tests to pass — more than 20% of optimal AND more than 0.8 km absolute. The absolute limb passes, but the percentage limb fails by a wide margin, so no deviation is established and, under POL-RD-01, the outcome is NO_ACTION however the trip is characterised. POL-RD-02's optimal-route recomputation is therefore never reached and no part of the contested 76.88 has an arithmetic basis. The present state of the ledger stands: payment_status CHARGED, refund_issued_sgd 0.00.\n\nThe rider's concern that she was 'charged for everybody's trip' is answered by POL-RD-12: a pooled route is longer by construction, the co-riders' collection and set-down legs are part of the matched itinerary and are excluded from excess precisely by using that baseline, and the policy provides no distance refund for the length of a pooled route the rider chose. The '174 dollar' figure in the claim finds no support on any artifact — the fare ledger's charged_total is 76.88, computed as base 3.80 + 0.75 x 60.9 km (45.68) + 0.28 x 95.0 min (26.60) + 0.80 platform fee, with zero ERP, zero tolls, zero airport surcharge, zero waiting-time fee, zero promo and surge_multiplier 1.0 (read from the fare_breakdown).\n\nThe driver's counter-statement ('Pool routes are long; that's how pool works. The app splits the fare, not me') cites no evidence ID and so carries no weight under POL-RD-08; it is not needed, because the rider's own threshold showing fails. The missing traffic