n a trip originating at NTU Hall 8, and no charge line without a counterpart, so nothing is refundable as a standalone correction. On trace integrity: EV-GPS-00527 is COMPLETE at weight 1.0 with 571 fixes at a 10 s cadence, 100% coverage, an empty gaps list and max_gap_sec 0.0, so it meets none of the POL-RD-07(a)–(c) impairment limbs; the finding that no deviation exists rests on that trace (weight 1.0) and the trip record (weight 1.0), and confidence is above the 0.70 floor. The missing traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-00527-01 (status MISSING, weight_multiplier 0.0, issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT) is disclosed, but neither party asserts an external traffic cause — the driver's statement is that pool routes are simply long — so no exculpatory clause is invoked against it, the absence decides nothing, and it does not trigger POL-RD-10(5) or a POL-RD-13 escalation. The driver's counterparty statement that 'pool routes are long; that's how pool works. The app splits the fare, not me' is consistent with the record, but I have not needed to rely on it; the outcome turns on the measured figures. On the profiles: only the fields POL-GEN-01 makes citable were consulted — rider_profile.deviation_claims_60d is 0 (so POL-RD-08's aggravated-corroboration condition is not met), and driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 0 against completed_trips_90d of 250 (so no POL-RD-06 pattern arises); every other profile field is context only and none was used to establish any fact about this trip. No POL-RD-10 escalation trigger fires, and no clause produces a referral on these facts. The present state of the ledger is left as it stands: payment_status CHARGED, refund_issued_sgd 0.00."
